docs/arnold/megaplan-native-semantic-parity-master-plan.md:958:## 6. Red Team: False Closure Routes and Patches
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-semantic-parity-master-plan.md:962:| Run `arnold workflow check` and claim success because it calls `check_workflow_file(..., evidence=None)`. | S1a closeout requires strict checker command and rejects non-strict CLI output. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-semantic-parity-master-plan.md:963:| Add row evidence records manually without source spans or hashes. | S1a/S7 require checker-generated JSON with row IDs, spans, source hashes, carrier class. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-semantic-parity-master-plan.md:966:| Cite `_compatibility.py` `NativeProgram` as native authority. | S1a/S6/S7 checker rejects compatibility projection evidence. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-semantic-parity-master-plan.md:971:| Mutate old carriers in a way tests never exercise. | Each mutation gate must run the relevant split-outcome scenarios with the old carrier disabled/deleted. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-semantic-parity-master-plan.md:972:| Shrink the row inventory so strict checking passes vacuously. | S1a/S7 require carrier-scan row registry reconciliation; every discovered carrier maps to a row or dated exemption, and S7 fails on unmapped carriers. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-semantic-parity-master-plan.md:973:| Narrow the carrier scan roots so hidden carriers sit outside scanned paths. | S1a/S7 scan package-wide roots with explicit exclusions; every exclusion requires dated exemption treatment and appears in the final report. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-semantic-parity-master-plan.md:974:| Rename or re-encode route carriers so token blacklist checks miss them. | S1a structural rejection and renamed-carrier fixtures detect route-shaped mappings, imported component callables, and dispatch tables regardless of name. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-semantic-parity-master-plan.md:976:| Edit a negative fixture so it still fails, but for a weaker unrelated diagnostic. | Permanent CI fixtures assert exact diagnostic codes, and checker meta-tests run in every sprint exit gate. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-semantic-parity-master-plan.md:977:| Compare "unchanged" behavior against the current post-extraction build. | S1a freezes golden split-outcome baselines before extraction; later mutation/parity gates diff against those baselines. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-semantic-parity-master-plan.md:979:| Regenerate baselines after extraction so parity trivially passes. | Baselines are write-once after each freeze; amendments require a separate reviewed ledger entry and S7 verifies hashes against the freeze record and ledger. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-semantic-parity-master-plan.md:980:| Exempt every inconvenient carrier from the row registry. | Exemptions have categories; scheduled exemptions must close by their sprint; S7 publishes exemption counts/diffs and fails on open scheduled exemptions. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-semantic-parity-master-plan.md:985:| Bury hundreds of route-shaped candidates under generic carrier exemptions. | S1a carrier tiering separates route-authoritative carriers from descriptive metadata, and route-authoritative carriers need row mapping or removal. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-semantic-parity-master-plan.md:986:| Run installed-package mode against checkout paths. | S1a installed-package checker must load `.pypeline` source through package resources from the installed artifact. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-semantic-parity-master-plan.md:989:| Misclassify live route authority as descriptive metadata. | S1/S7 seeded descriptive-carrier corruption must leave behavior unchanged; one behavior-changing sample invalidates the tier classification run. |
docs/arnold/megaplan-native-semantic-parity-master-plan.md:990:| The epic modifies the runner driving itself and loses the enforcement loop. | S0 pins the runner; repins happen only after S1b-2 and S5 with auto-drive characterization, strict checker, and North Star action smoke gates. |
